sre9018@csseq.tamu.edu (Steven Ray Evatt) writes:

{S} Unix NetHack Version 3.0i Patchlevel 9 - last build ...

{S} Well, I just died because I etched a wand in a shop, and it
{S} was identified as detect secert doors.  (there were no secert
{S} doors in the shop!)  But the two large mimics in the room all
{S} of a sudden came after me.

Damn!  We must have been in the same shop!  How come I didn't see you there? :-)

Amazing.  I just ran across the *exact* same situation in a game I just finished
(died) too.  However, my story goes a bit further.

{S} Is this a feature or a bug?

Definately a feature.  Secret Door Detection shows you not only secret doors,
but other "hidden" things too.  Like traps and (unfortunately in shops) mimics.
I do believe that this should work for trappers and the like too.

About that game ...
(press 'n' now those who do not care to hear NetHack war stories)


Well I managed to get my butt out of the shop before the mimics got to me.
And they hid once more.  However, this time they were in different positions
and standing on items.  So the old "step-in/step-out" trick no longer revealed
their position in the shop.  Ah well, I was broke and couldn't do much more
with the shop anyway.  So I went on exploring.

I explored the next level, and found a chest with a wand and a spellbook.
There was also some gold on the level.  "Well", I though to myself "that
shopkeeper (general store) will give me money for this spellbook".  So I
went back up to look around some more.

Now back in the shop again, I decided to test my new wand.  There were unknown
scrolls and the open door.  The shopkeeper was out of the way so I tried
zapping my wand across the scrolls at the open door to see what kind it was.
Suddenly the two mimics appear again!  The were between me and the door!
Now that wand wasn't secret door detection (I had already identified that one).
It was cancellation!  Ack!

Well this time I was trapped.  Luckily my spellbook was "to much to comprehend"
and it teleported me out of the shop.  However, the mimics were now forever
cancelled and would no longer hide at all.  So I abandoned the level until
I could come back and beat them.

I died several levels later, and never was able to return.

